      "writtenOn": "2024-04-25T22:53:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like we could try this first:\n```\nif (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NEED_SG_DMA_FLAGS))\n\treturn sg_dma_is_swiotlb(table-\u003esgl);\n```\n\nBut the direct path appears to be broken and needs a fix like this: aosp/3063405\n\nAnd drivers would also need to update to be sure they call `sg_dma_mark_swiotlb` as appropriate, otherwise this check won\u0027t work correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "02920e89_d356a169",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
