    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fedd7e1d_4e5a6cbd",
        "filename": "drivers/dma-buf/heaps/system_heap.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1930620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-29T20:43:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Conceptually I think the direct DMA path should set it.\n`iommu_dma_map_sg` uses `dev_use_sg_swiotlb` to decide to take `iommu_dma_map_sg_swiotlb` where `sg_dma_mark_swiotlb` is called. However there isn\u0027t currently an equivalent check for `dma_direct_map_sg`, so `dma_direct_map_page` is the only place where it\u0027s currently known if `swiotlb_map` will be called or not in the direct DMA path. So we could try to move the SWIOTLB checks from `dma_direct_map_page` to a similar helper function like `dev_use_sg_swiotlb` in order to not duplicate the checks.\nI think `dev_use_sg_swiotlb` is also a little bit broken though, because it doesn\u0027t respect the `force_bounce` flag in `struct device`, so I also had to make this change to test with the IOMMU path:\n```\n+++ b/drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c\n@@ -633,6 +633,7 @@ static bool dev_use_sg_swiotlb(struct device *dev, struct scatterlist *sg,\n                                return true;\n        }\n \n+       if (dev-\u003edma_io_tlb_mem) return dev-\u003edma_io_tlb_mem-\u003eforce_bounce;\n        return false;\n }\n```",
      "parentUuid": "42f61b42_50214ec1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "4575c060464b2b8e7d236daaff296482543e3d41",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8f3f95d_bc13ba6a",
        "filename": "drivers/dma-buf/heaps/system_heap.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-29T23:02:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that the direct DMA path should be calling `sg_dma_mark_swiotlb()`. I like the idea of moving those checks out to a helper function. We can make the code behave similarly to the dma-iommu path as long as it ends up cleaning up the direct DMA code.\n\nMy earlier comment was just that if we set the flag in the direct DMA path, and our only justification is so we can do it to support an out of tree feature (uncached system heap), then that may lower the patch\u0027s chances of being accepted.\n\nGood catch on not honoring the `force_bounce` usage on the dma-iommu path. Might be a good idea to submit that as a bug fix?",
      "parentUuid": "fedd7e1d_4e5a6cbd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "4575c060464b2b8e7d236daaff296482543e3d41",
